  "reason": "The abstract discusses the potential and challenges of using New Approach Methodologies (NAMs) in drug development, particularly for cardiac toxicity. It mentions that 'Case studies where NAMs offered superior predictivity compared to traditional methods are emerging', but it does not report any quantitative measure of agreement (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity/specificity) between non-human animal results and human clinical results. The focus is on the development and validation of NAMs themselves, not on a quantitative comparison of animal model performance against human outcomes."
